  "question": {
    "text": "Experimentally it was found that a metal oxide has formula <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0.98</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Metal M, present as <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> and <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> in its oxide. Fraction of the metal which exists as <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> would be nearly<br />\r[Report your answer by rounding it upto nearset whole number]",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "For a one mole of the oxide<br /><br />Moles of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.98</mn><mo>,</mo></math> Moles of <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><br />Let moles of <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math><br /><br />Moles of <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.98</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math><br /><br />on balancing charge<br /><br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0.98</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.04</mn></math><br /><br />% of <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.04</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>0.98</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4.08</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">%</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">%</mi></math>",
